🚽 Test case: round-17 review finding #2 -- maxxing (sizeof)'s operand
🚽 must never be evaluated, matching C. Before this fix, a bare native
🚽 call as sizeof's direct operand reached get_expression_type(), whose
🚽 NODE_FUNC_CALL case unconditionally invoked native_call_peek() (which
🚽 actually calls the native) to discover its type -- even though Phase 2
🚽 (issue #205) already made a TYPED native's return type statically
🚽 knowable from its own StdrotEntry, with no execution required.
🚽 get_native_call_static_type() (ast.c) now answers this from the
🚽 descriptor alone; proven here by reading stdin exactly once, from the
🚽 SECOND (real, statement-position) slorp(x) call -- if maxxing(slorp(x))
🚽 had actually executed slorp, it would have consumed the one line of
🚽 stdin this test provides, leaving nothing for the second call to read.
skibidi main {
    rizz x = 0;
    rizz n = maxxing(slorp(x));
    yapping("%d", n);
    rizz y = slorp(x);
    yapping("%d", y);
    bussin 0;
}
